# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 001
# Act: NUL+  (Void aimed at Figure)   Stance: Dissecting   Site: Entity
#
# The one operation, second use: a FIGURE against turn 0's ground — the
# first genuine Secondness, a brute dyadic fact. Not "there is no ground"
# (turn 0) but "THIS particular slot is empty" — a specific, nameable
# absence read against a ground that already exists to be empty relative
# to. In Spencer-Brown's terms: turn 0 was the unmarked state itself;
# this is the first crossing drawn against it — cross(void) = mark.
#
# Earning argument: NUL+ has exactly one precondition — a ground already
# constructed to register absence against (turn 0). SEED.md's Existence
# triad names this precisely: NUL "makes the space"; this act is NUL
# again, now aimed at a figure rather than at the ground in general, so
# it is not a new operator being introduced early — it is the same
# operator's second use, dependency-satisfied by its first.
#
# Refuted if: this act could be performed with turn 0 absent. It cannot
# — "aimed at Figure" presupposes a Ground the figure is read against,
# by construction, not by convention.

:turn-1  eot:opens        :turn-0 .
:turn-1  eot:act          eot:NUL+ .
:turn-1  eot:stance       "Dissecting" .
:turn-1  eot:site         "Entity" .
:turn-1  eot:target       "customer:123.preferred_contact" .
:turn-1  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 0.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
